# FocusLock: Project Dependency Graph & Structural Map

This document provides a **Graph-Aware Architectural Analysis** of the FocusLock codebase. It maps the dependencies, data flows, and structural relationships across the Clean Architecture layers, highlighting the completed elements and integrating the upcoming Phase 3 services.

---

## 1. High-Level Architectural Layers

The FocusLock Android app follows **Clean Architecture** combined with **MVVM**. The dependencies flow inward towards the Domain layer (which holds the pure business logic).

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph UI ["UI & Presentation Layer (Jetpack Compose)"]
        Screens[Screens & Composables] --> VM[ViewModels]
    end

    subgraph Domain ["Domain Layer (Business Logic & Rules)"]
        VM --> UseCases[Use Cases]
        UseCases --> RepoInterfaces[Repository Interfaces]
        UseCases --> DomModels[Domain Models]
    end

    subgraph Data ["Data Layer (Data Source & Persistence)"]
        RepoImpls[Repository Implementations] -.->|Implements| RepoInterfaces
        RepoImpls --> LocalDS[Local Data Source - Room DB]
        RepoImpls --> RemoteDS[Remote Data Source - Retrofit API]
    end

    subgraph DI ["Dependency Injection (Hilt)"]
        HiltModules[Hilt Modules] -->|Provides/Binds| RepoImpls
        HiltModules -->|Injects| VM
        HiltModules -->|Injects| UseCases
    end

    style UI fill:#2c3e50,stroke:#34495e,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff
    style Domain fill:#27ae60,stroke:#2ecc71,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff
    style Data fill:#8e44ad,stroke:#9b59b6,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff
    style DI fill:#d35400,stroke:#e67e22,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff
```

---

## 2. Complete Phase 2 Data Flow (Onboarding & Verification)

This graph traces the exact data flow during the onboarding and trusted contact registration phases.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as User
    participant Screen as TrustedContactSetupScreen
    participant VM as TrustedContactSetupViewModel
    participant UC as SaveTrustedContactUseCase
    participant Repo as TrustedContactRepositoryImpl
    participant API as FocusLockApi (Retrofit)
    participant DB as FocusDatabase (Room)

    User->>Screen: Enters Phone Number
    Screen->>VM: onSendOtpClicked(phone)
    VM->>UC: execute(phone)
    Note over UC: Trims, normalizes &<br/>validates E.164 phone format
    UC->>API: verifyContact(VerifyContactRequest)
    API-->>UC: Return Success (OTP Sent)
    UC->>Repo: saveTrustedContact(phone)
    Repo->>DB: Insert TrustedContactEntity
    Note over DB: Enforces max 1 row constraint
    Repo-->>UC: Done
    UC-->>VM: Success State
    VM-->>Screen: Navigate to VerifyContactScreen
```

---

## 3. Detailed Component & File Relationships

The following graph maps all physical Kotlin files in the repository and their explicit dependencies:

```mermaid
classDiagram
    class MainActivity {
        +onCreate()
    }
    class AppNavigation {
        <<navigation>>
        +NavHost()
    }
    
    class OnboardingScreen {
        <<ui>>
    }
    class OnboardingViewModel {
        -checkOnboardingStatusUseCase
    }
    
    class PermissionSetupScreen {
        <<ui>>
    }
    class PermissionSetupViewModel {
        -permissionChecker
    }
    
    class TrustedContactSetupScreen {
        <<ui>>
    }
    class TrustedContactSetupViewModel {
        -saveTrustedContactUseCase
    }
    
    class VerifyContactScreen {
        <<ui>>
    }
    class VerifyContactViewModel {
        -verifyContactOtpUseCase
    }

    class InitializeAppUseCase {
        -appSettingsRepository
        -blockingRepository
        +execute()
    }
    class CheckOnboardingStatusUseCase {
        -appSettingsRepository
        +execute()
    }
    class SaveTrustedContactUseCase {
        -trustedContactRepository
        -api
        +execute()
    }
    class VerifyContactOtpUseCase {
        -trustedContactRepository
        -api
        +execute()
    }

    class SessionRepository {
        <<interface>>
    }
    class BlockingRepository {
        <<interface>>
    }
    class TrustedContactRepository {
        <<interface>>
    }
    class UnlockRepository {
        <<interface>>
    }
    class AppSettingsRepository {
        <<interface>>
    }

    class SessionRepositoryImpl {
        -sessionDao
    }
    class BlockingRepositoryImpl {
        -blockedDomainDao
        -blockedKeywordDao
    }
    class TrustedContactRepositoryImpl {
        -trustedContactDao
    }
    class UnlockRepositoryImpl {
        -unlockRequestDao
    }
    class AppSettingsRepositoryImpl {
        -appSettingDao
    }

    MainActivity --> AppNavigation
    AppNavigation --> OnboardingScreen
    AppNavigation --> PermissionSetupScreen
    AppNavigation --> TrustedContactSetupScreen
    AppNavigation --> VerifyContactScreen

    OnboardingScreen --> OnboardingViewModel
    PermissionSetupScreen --> PermissionSetupViewModel
    TrustedContactSetupScreen --> TrustedContactSetupViewModel
    VerifyContactScreen --> VerifyContactViewModel

    OnboardingViewModel --> CheckOnboardingStatusUseCase
    TrustedContactSetupViewModel --> SaveTrustedContactUseCase
    VerifyContactViewModel --> VerifyContactOtpUseCase

    CheckOnboardingStatusUseCase --> AppSettingsRepository
    SaveTrustedContactUseCase --> TrustedContactRepository
    VerifyContactOtpUseCase --> TrustedContactRepository

    SessionRepositoryImpl ..|> SessionRepository
    BlockingRepositoryImpl ..|> BlockingRepository
    TrustedContactRepositoryImpl ..|> TrustedContactRepository
    UnlockRepositoryImpl ..|> UnlockRepository
    AppSettingsRepositoryImpl ..|> AppSettingsRepository

    RepositoryModule --> SessionRepositoryImpl : binds
    RepositoryModule --> BlockingRepositoryImpl : binds
    RepositoryModule --> TrustedContactRepositoryImpl : binds
    RepositoryModule --> UnlockRepositoryImpl : binds
    RepositoryModule --> AppSettingsRepositoryImpl : binds
```

